    2. Generate a single connected grey wall network on the grid with 1-cell-wide constraint (no 2x2 grey). Use a random walk / spanning-tree approach starting from a random cell, growing grey paths that branch and meander. Target grey fraction ~35-44%.
    3. Compute all 4-connected BLACK components. Require 7-8 regions with unique min and unique max area, and min != max.
    4. If constraints not met, retry from step 2 (or adjust wall placement).
    5. Input is the BLACK+GREY grid. Output is produced by coloring smallest region ORANGE, largest TEAL.
