38: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
39:     """
40:     Draw upward routes from the bottom markers, passing under exposed orange cells and stopping below orange roof notches.
41: 
42:     Input structure
43:     - The background is the dominant color.
44:     - One marker color appears only as one or more bottom-edge pixels.
45:     - The other foreground color forms orange obstacle pixels that the routes climb toward.
46: 
47:     Rule
48:     - From each bottom marker, move upward in its current column to the nearest orange pixel in the original input.
49:     - If that orange pixel roofs a one-cell notch, paint the vertical approach red and put a new marker in the notch below it.
50:     - Otherwise recolor the hit orange pixel teal, mark the cell below it yellow, draw red under the rest of its rightward row-run, mark the exit cell green, and continue upward from that exit column.
51:     - If no orange pixel remains above the current column, paint red up to the top edge and put a new marker on the top edge.
52: 
53:     Key insight
54:     - The route is a deterministic upward scan on the original orange mask; each exposed hit exits just to the right of the contiguous orange run on that row.
